[36m(PPOTrainer pid=3806248)[0m INFO 03-02 17:07:21 ppo_trainer.py:457] [trace] step=55 reward=0.000 response_len=5055 total_len=9082 preview='system name=<|plugin|>\\nYou are an expert reasoner with extensive experience in all areas. You approach problems through systematic thinking and rigorous reasoning. Your response should reflect deep understanding and precise logical thinking, making your solution path and reasoning clear to others. Please put your thinking process within <think>...</think> tags.\\n\\nYour response should consist of a reasoning step (**thought**) followed immediately by a function call in valid JSON format. Wrap each function call using the `<|action_start|><|plugin|>` and `<|action_end|>` tags.\\n\\n**Format example:**\\n\\n```\\n(Your thought goes here...)\\n\\n<|action_start|><|plugin|>\\n{\\n    "name": "tool_name",\\n    "parameters": {\\n        "parameter1": "value1",\\n        "parameter2": "value2"\\n    }\\n}\\n<|action_end|>\\n```\\n\\n# External Tools\\nYou have access to these tools:\\n[\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the average molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_exact_molecular_weight",\\n      "description": "Return the monoisotopic exact molecular weight (Daltons).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_heavy_atom_count",\\n      "description": "Return the number of non-hydrogen atoms (heavy atoms).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_logp",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen cLogP (octanol/water).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_tpsa",\\n      "description": "Return topological polar surface area TPSA (Å^2).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hbd",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond donors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_hba",\\n      "description": "Return Lipinski H-bond acceptors count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_rotatable_bonds",\\n      "description": "Return rotatable bonds count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_csp3",\\n      "description": "Return FractionCSP3 = (# sp3 carbon atoms)/(# total carbon atoms), Often used as a simple “3D character / saturation” proxy from 2D structure.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_mol_mr",\\n      "description": "Return Wildman–Crippen molar refractivity (MR).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_ring_count",\\n      "description": "Return total ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aromatic_rings",\\n      "description": "Return aromatic ring count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_formal_charge",\\n      "description": "Return net formal charge (sum of atom formal charges as encoded in the SMILES).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_qed",\\n      "description": "Return QED (Quantitative Estimate of Drug-likeness) as implemented in RDKit.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_heteroatoms",\\n      "description": "Return heteroatom count (non C/H).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "describe_high_level_fg_fragments",\\n      "description": "Accurately parse functional groups with attachment points, corresponding fragment SMILES, and atom ids in the SMILES string for better structure description.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "The SMILES string to parse."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ]\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "remove_salts",\\n      "description": "Desalt a SMILES by removing salts/counterions and keeping ONLY the largest organic fragment. Use this tool when the SMILES contains multiple disconnected components separated by \'.\' and one or more components are likely inorganic ions/solvents (e.g., [Na+], Cl-, Br-, I-, [K+], [Li+], [Ca2+], [Mg2+], [NH4+], sulfate/phosphate, etc.), or when you want the parent (active) molecule for downstream property prediction.\\nIn aqueous/physiological conditions, salts typically dissociate; counterions are usually not part of the parent drug structure for many structure-based predictions.\\nTypical examples needing desalting: \'CC(=O)O.[Na+]\', \'[Na+].O=C(O)c1ccccc1\', \'CCO.Cl\'.\\nDo NOT use if the SMILES is already a single component (no \'.\') or if multiple organic fragments represent real mixture/co-crystal/combination therapy that should be kept. Output is the canonical SMILES of the retained parent fragment; smaller fragments are discarded.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "predict_pka",\\n      "description": "Predict pKa values for ionizable sites in a molecule. Returns base-site and acid-site pKa values (1-indexed atom map numbers), the most basic/acidic pKa, the number of basic/acidic sites, and the atom-mapped SMILES.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "estimate_logd",\\n      "description": "Estimate logD at a target pH from predicted pKa values and RDKit logP. Uses a Henderson-Hasselbalch approximation: logD(pH) ≈ logP + log10(f_neutral). logP is RDKit Wildman-Crippen logP. This is a heuristic intended for helpingyour reasoning and should not be treated as experimental logD. For polyprotic molecules, uses the most basic and most acidic predicted pKa values.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "ph": {\\n            "type": "number",\\n            "description": "Target pH (default: 7.4)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "score_structural_alerts",\\n      "description": "Screen a molecule against RDKit\'s built-in structural alert catalogs (PAINS, Brenk, NIH, ZINC, ChEMBL, etc.).",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          },\\n          "alert_library": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "enum": [\\n              "all",\\n              "pains",\\n              "pains_a",\\n              "pains_b",\\n              "pains_c",\\n              "brenk",\\n              "nih",\\n              "zinc",\\n              "chembl",\\n              "chembl_bms",\\n              "chembl_lint",\\n              "chembl_mlsmr"\\n            ],\\n            "description": "Alert library to screen against (default: all)."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_fraction_aromatic_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return fraction of aromatic atoms.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_num_aromatic_atoms",\\n      "description": "Return aromatic atom count.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_max_abs_partial_charge",\\n      "description": "Return max absolute Gasteiger partial charge.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_min_abs_partial_charge",\\n      "description": "Return min absolute Gasteiger partial charge.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_max_estate_index",\\n      "description": "Return max EState index among atoms.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_min_estate_index",\\n      "description": "Return min EState index among atoms.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_bertz_ct",\\n      "description": "Return Bertz complexity index.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  },\\n  {\\n    "type": "function",\\n    "function": {\\n      "name": "get_balaban_j",\\n      "description": "Return Balaban J topological index.",\\n      "parameters": {\\n        "type": "object",\\n        "properties": {\\n          "smiles": {\\n            "type": "string",\\n            "description": "SMILES string of the molecule."\\n          }\\n        },\\n        "required": [\\n          "smiles"\\n        ],\\n        "additionalProperties": false\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n]\\nuser\\nInstructions: Answer the following question about drug properties.\\nContext: Mutagenicity means the ability of a drug to induce genetic alterations. Drugs that can cause damage to the DNA can result in cell death or other severe adverse effects. Nowadays, the most widely used assay for testing the mutagenicity of compounds is the Ames experiment which was invented by a professor named Ames. The Ames test is a short-term bacterial reverse mutation assay detecting a large number of compounds which can induce genetic damage and frameshift mutations.\\nQuestion: Given a drug SMILES string, predict whether it\\n(A) is not mutagenic (B) is mutagenic\\nDrug SMILES: C/C=C1/C[C@H](C)[C@](O)(CO)C(=O)OCC2=CC[N@@+]3([O-])CC[C@@H](OC1=O)[C@@H]23Please think step by step and use tools when helpful. Then put your final choice ((A) or (B)) after "Answer:"\\nassistant\\n<think>\\nThe user asks to predict mutagenicity for a given SMILES. We need to output either (A) not mutagenic or (B) mutagenic. We have tools for various molecular properties but not directly for mutagenicity prediction. However, we can use tools to compute properties that might correlate with mutagenicity, such as structural alerts, functional groups, etc. The tools include "score_structural_alerts" which can screen against PAINS, Brenk, NIH, ZINC, ChEMBL etc. Some of these might indicate mutagenic alerts. Also, we can compute other descriptors like logP, TPSA, etc., but mutagenicity is often associated with certain structural features like aromatic amines, nitro groups, epoxides, etc. We need to analyze the SMILES.\\n\\nLet\'s first parse the SMILES: "C/C=C1/C[C@H](C)[C@](O)(CO)C(=O)OCC2=CC[N@@+]3([O-])CC[C@@H](OC1=O)[C@@H]23". It looks complex with stereochemistry. It appears to be a lactone or macrocycle with an oxygen bridge, maybe a macrolide? There\'s an [N@@+]3([O-]) which suggests a nitro group or nitroso? Actually it\'s a charged nitrogen with oxygen negative, maybe a nitro group in a cyclic system? Let\'s examine: "CC2=CC[N@@+]3([O-])CCC..." This could be a nitro group attached to a nitrogen in a ring? Might be a nitroalkane or nitroso. Nitro groups are often associated with mutagenicity (nitroarenes, nitroheterocycles). Also, there is an ester group C(=O)OCC2=... and a lactone ring (OC1=O). The molecule might be a macrolide antibiotic? Some macrolides are not mutagenic, but some nitro-containing compounds are mutagenic.\\n\\nWe can use the functional group analysis tool to identify potential mutagenic fragments. Let